/-!
# Lower order bound for the literal max2 quotient subgroup

The explicit quotient matrices act on row vectors on the right. Three checked
orbit trees provide 2016 cosets of the stabilizer of row 1, 165 cosets of the
additional stabilizer of row 2533, and 8 distinct elements of the latter.
Their product is 2661120. Every matrix identity, generator word, tree edge and
distinctness certificate is checked by Lean's kernel.

This proves only a lower bound for the literal subgroup generated by
`quotientX` and `quotientY`. Its source-to-quotient comparison is separate.
Source motivation: GLS3, Table 5.3i, printed p.270; see
`QuotientOrder/source/README.md` for attribution and reproducibility.
-/

namespace Janko4.OuterReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.TwoCoreCentralizerData.LowerBound

public theorem quotientSubgroup_card_ge : 2661120 ≤ Nat.card quotientSubgroup := by
  have h0 := QuotientOrderCertificate.level0_bound
  have h1 := QuotientOrderCertificate.level1_bound
  have h2 := QuotientOrderCertificate.level2_bound
  omega

end Janko4.OuterReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.TwoCoreCentralizerData.LowerBound
